# Magda attacks on turns 3, 5, 7 and 9 and each tap makes a Treasure (the Dwarf that becomes tapped is Magda herself). With four
# Treasures on turn 9 "Sacrifice five Treasures" is not offered (the refusal); on turn 11 a fifth tap makes it payable and
# Bot1 sacrifices all five to search for an artifact or Dragon card: it may find Kokusho, the Evening Star (a Dragon, not an
# artifact) but not a Mountain (the refusal), and the card goes onto the battlefield.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Magda, Brazen Outlaw
Mountain x4
Mountain x5
Kokusho, the Evening Star
Sol Ring
Mountain x8

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Magda, Brazen Outlaw.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Magda, Brazen Outlaw > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Magda, Brazen Outlaw > Bot2)
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Magda, Brazen Outlaw > Bot2)
[T9 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Magda, Brazen Outlaw > Bot2)
[T9 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token#4.Types = Artifact
! Bot1.Battlefield.Magda, Brazen Outlaw.Activate
[T11 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Magda, Brazen Outlaw > Bot2)
[T11 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Magda, Brazen Outlaw.Activate
! Bot1.Search(Mountain)
Bot1.Search(Kokusho, the Evening Star)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Kokusho, the Evening Star.Types = Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 4
Bot2.Life = 10
